==German==

===Etymology===
From {{inh|de|gmh|topf}}, from (western) {{inh|de|goh|*topf}}, {{m|goh|*tupf}}, from {{inh|de|gem-pro|*duppaz|t=hollow, bowl}}, from {{der|de|ine-pro|*dʰewb-|t=deep, hollow}}. Probably related to English {{m|en|dop||a cup in which a diamond is cut}} and {{cog|nl|dop||a little cup, a thimble}}.

